e67997dc8 timed one COLD dispatch per arm (`test` mode + GGML_VK_PERF_LOGGER) because the brief's
shape was missing from perf mode's own case list. Adding it there (tests/test-backend-ops.cpp
:12040-12046) and re-running the brief's instrument — 22-30 dispatches averaged, 6 interleaved
rounds — changes two of three conclusions. The single-dispatch figures are withdrawn, not amended:
~58 ms cold against perf's ~35 ms is a different measurement, not a noisier one.

perf mode, 6 interleaved rounds, m=17408 n=512 k=5120 (r52b-evidence/25-perfmode-6rounds.txt):

  A1 S-X8 mul_mm packed=0   35169 us median  [34111 .. 36026]
  A2 S-X8 mul_mm packed=1   34753 us median  [33436 .. 47784]   -1.18%, ranges OVERLAP = TIE
  A0 q8_0 mul_mm control    41511 us median  [40270 .. 73669]
  B  S-X8 MMQ under coopmat 46348 us median  [45038 .. 52746]   +31.79% vs A1, NON-OVERLAPPING
  B  q8_0 MMQ under coopmat 35979 us median  [35493 .. 37753]   -13.33% vs A0, NON-OVERLAPPING

WHAT CHANGED:

- q8_0 integer MMQ under coopmat is a WIN, not a loss. The coopmat arm's missing MMQ registrations
  cost q8_0 13% at prefill width on this device. WI-1724 is a LIVE lane, for q8_0.
- S-X8 integer MMQ still loses, and by more than anything else in the table (1.32x). Its fix is the
  tile decode, as briefed.
- The packed tile decode is a TIE at this shape, not a -2.20% win. It stays default-ON for RDNA3 on
  the distributable-engine ground — strictly fewer operations (16 -> 6 byte loads per 8 weights) for
  a bit-identical result, the ground GGML_VK_Q6K_DIRECT_SCALES stands on — and NO speed win may be
  quoted for it. A quiet-window re-pair is owed.

UNCHANGED: S-X8 mul_mm beats q8_0 mul_mm at this shape (-15.28%), so the brief's -22% premise is not
reproduced here; the coverage hole (no S-X8 MUL_MAT row above n=8 in either case list) and the
planted red stand as committed.

Report sections 0, 4 and 7 rewritten; both OPTIONS-REGISTRY evidence cells replaced; the superseded
receipt is kept in the tree and labelled as superseded rather than deleted.

Origin: fork-authored (ArifiLabs lane-243 R52b S-X8 coopmat mul_mm decode, Opus 5 MEDIUM kernel-maker)
Measured-effect: diagnostic only (one shape, perf mode, 6 interleaved rounds, receipts); HQ benches quiet
Lane: lane-243
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
